type CameraConfigOrigin string

// CameraConfigPatch Sparse change to the normalized model; omitted fields stay as they are. The fields that can
// be changed today are `detection.enabled` (boolean), `detection.objects` (raw engine object
// labels until the object catalog lands), `recording.enabled` (boolean), `analytics.lpr`
// (boolean) and `streams.primary` / `streams.detection`, each a sparse object with
// `resolution` ({width, height}), `fps`, `codec` (h264, h265, mjpeg, mpeg4), `bitrate_kbps`
// and `gop`. Stream fields are written to the camera over ONVIF; the detection stream's
// `resolution` and `fps` go to Frigate's detect section when it has no ONVIF profile of its
// own (see getCameraVideoOptions `apply_via`). The schema is deliberately open so the server can reject every other field,
// nested ones included, with 400 instead of dropping it silently.
//
// Example: {"analytics":{"lpr":false},"detection":{"enabled":true,"objects":["person","car"]},"recording":{"enabled":true}}
